Debug.Assert((RET + y) == x);
</code>

The assert statement corresponds to the comment that starts with "@@@". The assert statement accesses the value of the `RET` variable (which refers to the return value of the function), and compares it with the value of `x` after the increment operation. If the assertion is true, nothing happens. If the assertion fails, an AssertionFailedException is thrown.--------------------